## Build and push the image

The build context is the project root, because the image installs the project:

```shell
docker build -f {{ dockerfile_ref }} -t {{ image }} .
docker push {{ image }}
```

## Install the chart

```shell
helm install {{ name }} ./{{ chart_ref }} --namespace {{ namespace }} --create-namespace
```

The CRDs are installed from `crds/` before the operator starts. Helm never
upgrades or deletes that directory, so a CRD change has to be applied by hand:

```shell
kubectl apply -f {{ chart_ref }}/crds/
```

## Watch the operator

```shell
kubectl --namespace {{ namespace }} logs --follow deploy/{{ name }}-{{ chart_name }}
```
