## Admission webhooks

The webhook server is part of `based-operators` itself: the image runs the
operator with `kopf run ... -m {{ webhook_module }}`, and the module reads
everything deployment-specific from the environment the chart sets. All that is
needed alongside it is the deployment — a cert-manager `Certificate`, a `Service`
the API server can reach, and permission to manage the webhook configurations.

It needs [cert-manager](https://cert-manager.io/) in the cluster; point
`webhook.certManager.issuerRef` at your own CA-backed issuer to avoid the
self-signed one, or set `webhook.enabled=false` to deploy without webhooks.
